WEBVTT

00:11.011 --> 00:13.013
[rock music playing]

00:44.837 --> 00:46.589
WE WERE FRIENDS, EPISODE 4

00:46.672 --> 00:47.798
[exhales sharply]

00:48.632 --> 00:50.843
[chuckles]

00:51.969 --> 00:53.471
He's not gonna look for it.

00:53.554 --> 00:55.848
Math isn't going on the web novel website

00:55.931 --> 00:57.266
and searching

00:58.100 --> 00:59.977
for We Were Friends just to

01:00.561 --> 01:01.562
check this.

01:03.105 --> 01:04.523
He never would.

01:04.607 --> 01:07.067
[inhales sharply, sighs]

01:08.611 --> 01:09.612
[chuckles]

01:09.695 --> 01:10.696
PAZER WEB NOVEL PORTAL

01:10.780 --> 01:12.031
WE WERE FRIENDS

01:12.114 --> 01:15.826
WE WERE FRIENDS, EPISODE 4

01:17.620 --> 01:19.038
…YOON ONLY HAD EYES FOR TAE-HA…

01:28.005 --> 01:29.256
[scoffs]

01:29.340 --> 01:31.675
This girl is something else.

01:34.178 --> 01:35.221
[sighs]

01:39.058 --> 01:40.309
WE WERE FRIENDS, EPISODE 1

01:44.230 --> 01:45.231
WE WERE FRIENDS, EPISODE 2

01:47.191 --> 01:48.275
WE WERE FRIENDS, EPISODE 3

01:50.361 --> 01:52.780
END OF EPISODE 3

02:01.372 --> 02:04.834
CHAPTER 23: YOUR ROUGH THOUGHTS
AND ANXIOUS LOOKS

02:04.917 --> 02:07.545
[Woo-su chewing] Mmm. Mmm.

02:10.130 --> 02:12.341
EPISODE 7

02:14.176 --> 02:21.016
So, it turns out that the EBC people
are very excited about the math class too.

02:21.100 --> 02:22.810
[Gi-jeon, Dong-ju chuckling]

02:22.893 --> 02:26.522
No wonder. I'd be excited too.
I mean, it's the elite math genius' class.

02:26.605 --> 02:29.233
-[chuckles] Isn't that right? Right?
-Mm-hmm. Mmm.

02:30.234 --> 02:32.653
Of course, I respect your decision.

02:32.736 --> 02:33.946
You don't have to feel burdened at all.

02:34.029 --> 02:36.448
-Not at all.
-Mmm! That's right.

02:36.532 --> 02:39.785
But you're human,
and maybe you changed your mind, right?

02:39.869 --> 02:42.955
So, let me ask one last time,
did you perhaps change your mind…

02:43.038 --> 02:44.039
Uh, no?

02:46.250 --> 02:47.334
[door closes]

02:48.294 --> 02:49.837
-Do something.
-[Gi-jeon groans]

02:59.680 --> 03:00.764
[Young-hee] Today's the day.

03:00.848 --> 03:06.145
Therefore, I'm going to ask you
that until the filming is over

03:06.228 --> 03:09.440
and until EBC production crew
leaves the school,

03:09.523 --> 03:10.983
please stay focused

03:11.066 --> 03:14.862
and refrain from saying anything
that may work against our school.

03:15.696 --> 03:19.658
And I will ask,
especially the homeroom teachers,

03:19.742 --> 03:22.036
to please make sure
you keep the students attire

03:22.119 --> 03:24.413
and behavior under control.

03:24.997 --> 03:29.418
That way, we will have successful
and smooth results!

03:29.501 --> 03:31.211
-[teacher 1] Yes, ma'am.
-[teacher 2] Yes, ma'am.

03:31.295 --> 03:35.799
Good luck, especially to our new teachers,
and the hero of this event,

03:35.883 --> 03:37.259
Mr. Ga Woo-su.

03:38.052 --> 03:42.389
♪ Good luck, Mr. Ga Woo-su ♪

03:42.473 --> 03:44.266
-Yes.
-Please do a good job.

03:45.351 --> 03:48.354
You can do it!

03:49.480 --> 03:51.565
Mr. Da-ju, are you sure about this?

03:51.649 --> 03:54.985
Yes, all roads lead to Seoul.
Isn't that right, ma'am?

03:55.069 --> 03:57.321
Mmm. [chuckles]

03:57.404 --> 04:00.532
-Auntie, Auntie!
-[cheers]

04:00.616 --> 04:02.409
Here comes our main character.

04:02.493 --> 04:05.621
Wow, Mr. E-den.
Look at that outfit. [gasps]

04:05.704 --> 04:08.791
Wow. You are born for the spotlight, huh?

04:08.874 --> 04:11.251
-Mr. Da-ju, I can always rely on you.
-[chuckling]

04:11.335 --> 04:13.212
-Yes.
-Good.

04:13.295 --> 04:14.630
Mmm.

04:14.713 --> 04:17.508
So you're our dear principal's nephew.
[chuckles]

04:17.591 --> 04:19.927
-[chuckles]
-[scoffs]

04:20.719 --> 04:22.721
[door opens, closes]

04:22.805 --> 04:23.806
[scoffs]

04:24.640 --> 04:28.018
Auntie, you do know what the highlight
of this shoot is, right?

04:28.102 --> 04:29.645
It's my flute solo.

04:29.728 --> 04:31.772
Up on stage, and the curtains open.

04:31.855 --> 04:34.400
Then a spotlight hits me perfectly.

04:34.483 --> 04:36.944
Ha. Then that's it. It's game over.

04:37.027 --> 04:40.364
-Sure, but drink this first. [chuckles]
-Okay.

04:41.573 --> 04:43.117
-Huh.
-What?

04:43.742 --> 04:45.369
[stammers]

04:48.330 --> 04:51.959
-This is one of my favorite coffee shops.
-Yes, I know.

04:52.042 --> 04:54.128
Drink it up.

04:54.211 --> 04:55.963
Uh-huh. A little more. More.

04:57.381 --> 05:00.134
A little more. More. More.

05:03.303 --> 05:04.471
[winces]

05:04.555 --> 05:07.016
[students chattering]

05:25.451 --> 05:27.161
-[imitates flute]
-I like that.

05:27.244 --> 05:29.830
What if I go on TV and become too popular
to be a teacher?

05:29.913 --> 05:32.207
-[laughs]
-[laughing] Oh, my god.

05:32.291 --> 05:36.712
Did you see how the newbies
got all dressed up for the shoot?

05:36.795 --> 05:37.921
[scoffs] Pathetic.

05:38.005 --> 05:41.884
All that preparation just to be
in a tiny corner of the background on TV.

05:41.967 --> 05:44.344
I feel really bad for them, though.

05:44.428 --> 05:47.056
-Exactly.
-[chuckles]

05:47.139 --> 05:49.683
Uh, this is not working fast enough.

05:49.767 --> 05:50.893
Huh? What was that?

05:52.561 --> 05:54.313
[exhales sharply] Oh.

05:58.192 --> 06:00.360
[gasps] I shouldn't waste time here.

06:00.444 --> 06:02.237
I better go out and rehearse
with the cameras.

06:02.321 --> 06:03.530
[sighs, gasps]

06:06.950 --> 06:08.160
Oh…

06:11.455 --> 06:15.918
I'm really sorry, E-den.

06:16.543 --> 06:17.753
Film him without knowing?

06:17.836 --> 06:18.962
[sighs]

06:19.046 --> 06:21.715
Don't put it that way. It sounds illegal.

06:22.299 --> 06:26.553
You'll just hit this button here
and turn the power on.

06:27.846 --> 06:30.516
And this thing
will automatically start filming him.

06:31.600 --> 06:32.601
I can't.

06:32.684 --> 06:35.187
I could never do that. [sighs]

06:35.270 --> 06:37.022
I've gotta keep a low profile, okay?

06:37.106 --> 06:39.358
If I cause any more trouble,
I'll end up serving time.

06:39.441 --> 06:40.734
Mm-mmm. Mmm. Mmm. Mm-hmm.

06:40.818 --> 06:42.027
Come on, sit down. Sit down.

06:42.861 --> 06:45.489
-[sighs]
-Come on, I get how mean Ga Woo-su is,

06:45.572 --> 06:47.616
but he's not sending a student to jail.

06:47.699 --> 06:51.286
And you need to do this to make up
for messing around in my class.

06:51.912 --> 06:53.747
The nerve you had
to write that in my class.

06:53.831 --> 06:55.499
Do you even know how hurt I was?

06:55.582 --> 06:59.753
Th-That… [sighs]
I'm really sorry about that, but…

07:01.213 --> 07:05.134
Of all the students here,
do you not get why I'm doing this?

07:05.217 --> 07:06.468
Nope.

07:08.303 --> 07:09.721
Well, if you don't do it…

07:11.515 --> 07:12.975
we'll all be fired.

07:13.058 --> 07:14.184
Do you get it?

07:14.268 --> 07:15.435
You're getting fired?

07:16.603 --> 07:19.064
This is a direct order from the principal.

07:19.857 --> 07:23.110
Do you know what happens
when someone goes against her will?

07:23.193 --> 07:24.862
We get fired.

07:24.945 --> 07:27.197
And for me? "Not a problem."

07:27.281 --> 07:28.532
[inhales sharply]

07:28.615 --> 07:29.616
But…

07:30.492 --> 07:34.454
it will be a problem for the PE
and Korean lit teachers.

07:36.498 --> 07:38.584
What about them?
What would happen to them?

07:39.459 --> 07:43.297
It won't be easy for Mr. Jung
to get hired given his leg issue.

07:44.506 --> 07:47.217
Oh, and Mr. Yoon… Yeah…

07:56.143 --> 07:57.144
Oh…

07:58.061 --> 07:59.354
That's not good at all.

07:59.438 --> 08:01.815
-That's right. It's not good.
-[sighs]

08:02.691 --> 08:04.109
And…

08:05.569 --> 08:06.820
I know everything, kid.

08:07.946 --> 08:10.115
-Know what?
-Come on, you know what.

08:10.824 --> 08:12.618
Do you have any idea how fast I caught on?

08:13.327 --> 08:15.078
I could tell right away. [scoffs]

08:15.162 --> 08:17.539
Did you actually think
you could hide it? [scoffs]

08:19.041 --> 08:21.960
Well, I don't quite follow. [chuckles]

08:23.712 --> 08:25.339
I knew about it all.

08:26.465 --> 08:27.591
From the beginning.

08:29.551 --> 08:31.428
Yeah, your rough thoughts

08:32.179 --> 08:33.347
and anxious looks.

08:33.430 --> 08:35.641
[scoffs] Mmm. I knew it all.

08:35.724 --> 08:37.100
[inhales sharply]

08:37.935 --> 08:39.144
I won't say a word

08:39.895 --> 08:40.938
if you do the filming.

08:41.021 --> 08:42.022
Okay?

08:48.570 --> 08:50.906
[sighs] How did he find out
I write novels?

08:53.242 --> 08:55.327
Girls, girls, girls.
What's all this chatter?

08:55.410 --> 08:58.080
You know what's going on.
We're shooting the TV show.

08:58.163 --> 09:00.707
[audio speeds up]

09:00.791 --> 09:03.293
You're the faces
of Murim Girls' High School.

09:03.919 --> 09:05.921
Come on, girls!

09:06.004 --> 09:07.839
I can't believe not even one of you is…

09:07.923 --> 09:09.466
[audio speeds up]

09:09.549 --> 09:11.260
All right, do one of your Spanish lessons.

09:11.343 --> 09:14.012
And you, solve some math problems.
Isn't that fun?

09:14.930 --> 09:15.931
Dear?

09:16.974 --> 09:17.975
Dear?

09:19.351 --> 09:20.602
Dear.

09:20.686 --> 09:21.853
Ji-a.

09:22.437 --> 09:23.563
Ji-a.

09:24.398 --> 09:26.775
Thank you, Jenny.

09:27.567 --> 09:28.610
And your uniform?

09:30.279 --> 09:32.322
-It's in the wash.
-Why?

09:33.031 --> 09:34.408
Why did you have to wash it

09:34.491 --> 09:36.785
when you obviously knew
you had to come to school?

09:37.577 --> 09:38.787
I spilled oil on it.

09:40.998 --> 09:43.709
You should have worn it
even if you had oil on it.

09:43.792 --> 09:46.086
Or you should have just taken it out
from the washing machine

09:46.169 --> 09:47.587
and worn it even if it was still wet.

09:47.671 --> 09:49.673
Why today of all days?

09:49.756 --> 09:50.757
And your gym clothes?

09:50.841 --> 09:51.842
Don't have them.

09:51.925 --> 09:54.678
Borrow them from someone else!

09:54.761 --> 09:55.929
Actually, no.

09:56.013 --> 09:57.931
No, that won't do. Hey, what's your name?

09:58.015 --> 09:59.099
Choi Ji-a.

09:59.182 --> 10:00.225
Follow me with your desk.

10:01.184 --> 10:02.894
Move it. You're going slow.

10:02.978 --> 10:04.646
We don't have time.

10:07.149 --> 10:08.150
What's going on?

10:08.734 --> 10:09.735
Oh…

10:09.818 --> 10:12.237
Mr. Ga. Uh…

10:12.321 --> 10:16.700
Well, you see, I'm going to have her
study alone in the counseling room

10:16.783 --> 10:17.993
until the fifth period.

10:18.076 --> 10:20.078
-Come on, grab your desk.
-[Woo-su] Go back in.

10:22.164 --> 10:23.415
Mr. Ga.

10:23.498 --> 10:26.793
Could I have a word
with you, please? [chuckles]

10:29.546 --> 10:32.674
You know, EBC is coming here
to film their show today.

10:32.758 --> 10:35.635
This lazy girl dozes off
during class all the time

10:35.719 --> 10:37.095
and she's not wearing her uniform.

10:37.179 --> 10:40.474
I know that's her thing.

10:40.557 --> 10:41.600
[clicks tongue, inhales sharply]

10:41.683 --> 10:45.020
But if she's going to ruin
this school's reputation on our big day,

10:45.103 --> 10:46.521
she's better off not here.

10:46.605 --> 10:50.275
I would freak out if they show her
on camera dressed like that.

10:50.901 --> 10:54.196
I don't think this TV show
is worth making a student invisible.

10:54.821 --> 10:58.200
Wow, you're kind of naive,
you know that, Mr. Ga?

10:58.283 --> 11:00.327
TV shows are all scripted anyway.

11:00.410 --> 11:02.037
Just until fifth period, okay?

11:02.120 --> 11:03.246
Dear.

11:03.330 --> 11:05.540
If you insist on removing her
from the show,

11:06.041 --> 11:09.294
I won't let any of my students
participate in the filming.

11:10.754 --> 11:11.922
[scoffs]

11:14.591 --> 11:15.884
Who are you to say that?

11:16.468 --> 11:17.886
[inhales sharply] Mr. Ga.

11:17.969 --> 11:20.680
I believe I've explained this enough
for you to understand by now.

11:22.182 --> 11:23.183
Come on.

11:23.809 --> 11:24.810
Move!

11:28.230 --> 11:29.314
[Young-hee sighs]

11:33.735 --> 11:35.320
[Young-hee breathes shakily]

11:35.904 --> 11:39.658
[straining]

11:39.741 --> 11:40.951
Oh, no.

11:41.952 --> 11:42.953
[gasps]

11:43.620 --> 11:45.789
I'll talk to you later, Mr. Ga. [chuckles]

11:45.872 --> 11:49.084
Yes, hi. I'm coming. [chuckles]

11:50.043 --> 11:52.295
Back inside. Everyone sit down.

11:58.218 --> 12:00.387
[pop music playing]

12:00.470 --> 12:04.933
CHAPTER 24:
OUR SCHOOL RIGHT NOW

12:19.322 --> 12:20.699
Hi, I'm Jenny.

12:20.782 --> 12:24.703
And I'm on an exchange student program
in Murim Girls' High School.

12:24.786 --> 12:26.663
Oh, I'm also from Singapore.

12:27.873 --> 12:30.750
Um, why did you choose Murim Girls' High?

12:30.834 --> 12:31.918
Oh, okay.

12:32.002 --> 12:36.006
So Murim Girls' High School
is super famous in Singapore.

12:36.089 --> 12:38.925
Internationally too, it's known to be
like a really good school.

12:39.009 --> 12:40.802
[chuckles] Uh, brag about our school? Uh…

12:40.886 --> 12:44.723
Yeah. Yeah, we have…
We have a really nice schoolyard.

12:44.806 --> 12:49.478
And… And our teachers…
Our teachers are super, super handsome.

12:49.561 --> 12:51.104
-Yep, that's for real.
-Mr. Yoon Dong-ju.

12:51.188 --> 12:52.606
There's a teacher named Jung Gi-jeon.

12:52.689 --> 12:55.442
-No. No. Mr. Yoon Dong-ju…
-Uh-uh, it's Mr. Jung.

12:56.526 --> 12:59.279
Mr. Noh, I can't do it. I really can't.

12:59.362 --> 13:00.572
[hisses]

13:00.655 --> 13:02.574
-Yes, you can do it. Yes.
-[sighs] No.

13:02.657 --> 13:04.326
Why do you even think
that you can't do it?

13:04.409 --> 13:06.036
Stop having such weak thoughts. Come on.

13:06.119 --> 13:08.747
You're a Murim girl
with endless potential, kid.

13:08.830 --> 13:10.040
-Yeah.
-What does that even have to…

13:10.123 --> 13:11.458
Oh. He's here. I'm leaving.

13:11.541 --> 13:13.210
And get the job done, okay?

13:16.087 --> 13:17.380
I'm watching you.

13:19.799 --> 13:22.177
[chuckles]

13:24.596 --> 13:25.764
Here's an easy one.

13:25.847 --> 13:29.434
From these conditions,
we can derive two distinct equations.

13:30.018 --> 13:31.937
-First, let's find the value of x…
-[sighs]

13:32.020 --> 13:34.397
[Eui-ju] He'll kill me
if he discovers that I'm filming him

13:34.481 --> 13:36.566
…the equation of this tangent line,
we can use it…

13:36.650 --> 13:39.361
But then he's exposed the fact
that I write novels

13:39.444 --> 13:41.780
after acting like he'd keep it a secret.

13:41.863 --> 13:43.532
So let's just do it.

13:43.615 --> 13:44.741
Mr. Ga.

13:47.244 --> 13:48.245
I…

13:48.787 --> 13:50.455
I have a question I'd like to ask.

13:53.083 --> 13:54.084
What is it?

13:57.212 --> 13:58.797
Uh…

13:58.880 --> 14:01.633
Uh… Mr. Ga,

14:01.716 --> 14:07.055
I heard you got faculty offers
from renowned overseas universities.

14:07.138 --> 14:09.182
Why did you decide to teach here then?

14:12.143 --> 14:13.520
Why are you asking this now?

14:15.981 --> 14:18.149
Because I've thought about it
since you got here.

14:18.775 --> 14:21.778
It's surprising a genius like you
chose to teach students here

14:21.861 --> 14:26.700
so I'm wondering
if there's a story behind it.

14:30.495 --> 14:33.290
I believe that's the type of question
you ask after class.

14:34.165 --> 14:35.917
-Oh, come on.
-[groans]

14:36.001 --> 14:38.169
-We wanna hear the story too.
-[groans]

14:38.253 --> 14:39.838
-Yes, I'm curious too.
-If you tell us the story,

14:39.921 --> 14:40.922
we'll study very hard!

14:41.006 --> 14:42.465
[students chanting] Tell us now!

14:42.549 --> 14:43.717
Tell us now!

14:43.800 --> 14:45.135
Tell us now!

14:45.218 --> 14:48.388
-Tell us now! Tell us now!
-Quiet down.

14:50.056 --> 14:52.892
All right. This story may actually
be of help to you

14:52.976 --> 14:54.603
in deciding which career
to choose in life.

14:58.732 --> 14:59.733
For the Olympiad,

14:59.816 --> 15:04.321
they select six students that have to
go through two rounds of training camp.

15:04.404 --> 15:06.323
On the day we arrived,
for the first round,

15:06.406 --> 15:09.326
after checking in,
a test was already waiting for us.

15:09.909 --> 15:11.119
That test… [sighs]

15:40.231 --> 15:41.733
[gasps]

15:48.365 --> 15:49.574
Take it out.

15:51.451 --> 15:52.661
Take it out now.

15:59.668 --> 16:00.877
[gasps]

16:05.131 --> 16:07.050
[student] Wow… [whispers indistinctly]

16:11.471 --> 16:13.348
Mr. Ga! Mr. Ga! Wait!

16:13.431 --> 16:16.476
The Japanese language teacher said
all the teachers would get fired

16:16.559 --> 16:19.354
if I didn't do it.
That's why I did it, Mr. Ga.

16:19.437 --> 16:21.648
Mr. Ga, please hear me out this once.

16:21.731 --> 16:24.025
I couldn't let
the teachers get fired, Mr. Ga.

16:24.109 --> 16:26.027
Please hear me out, Mr. Ga. I…

16:27.487 --> 16:31.074
Noh Da-ju, how could you use a student
to film me? Have you lost it?

16:35.203 --> 16:37.580
Mr. Ga Woo-su, can you please calm down

16:38.164 --> 16:39.207
so we can talk it out?

16:39.791 --> 16:41.960
Someone filmed you
behind your back? [chuckles]

16:42.043 --> 16:43.044
How could… [chuckles]

16:43.670 --> 16:45.588
…someone ever do that?

16:46.673 --> 16:48.675
Did you really have to shove a camera
in my face?

16:48.758 --> 16:50.802
-You of all people?
-Guys, guys. Stop.

16:50.885 --> 16:52.220
What's going on, huh?

16:52.303 --> 16:53.388
Hey.

16:53.471 --> 16:55.140
That was a long time ago.

16:55.223 --> 16:56.433
You've gotta get over it.

16:56.516 --> 16:57.934
You're still dwelling on that?

17:01.521 --> 17:03.773
Hey! Hey, hey, hey! Hey!

17:05.567 --> 17:07.110
[Young-hee] Mr. Ga Woo-su.

17:10.864 --> 17:12.574
Could I have a moment with you?

17:17.537 --> 17:18.538
[sighs]

17:19.289 --> 17:20.498
Woo-su.

17:22.125 --> 17:23.460
[sighs]

17:26.379 --> 17:28.798
-[groans]
-You're unbelievable.

17:28.882 --> 17:31.593
-Mr. Jung… [stammers]
-[sighs] This is nuts.

17:31.676 --> 17:32.677
W-What is it?

17:32.761 --> 17:35.346
Did something happen
to Mr. Ga in the past?

17:35.430 --> 17:36.890
[sighs, clicks tongue]

17:41.436 --> 17:43.021
I don't know the details.

17:44.147 --> 17:45.565
But when Woo-su was ten,

17:46.733 --> 17:49.694
after being on a TV show,
he ended up being stalked.

17:50.570 --> 17:51.988
That darn stalker

17:52.655 --> 17:54.783
would go to his school
and even to his house.

17:54.866 --> 17:57.243
He filmed him without him knowing
what was going on.

17:57.327 --> 17:58.703
It was a total mess.

17:58.787 --> 17:59.829
Later on,

18:01.414 --> 18:02.791
he kidnapped Woo-su.

18:04.250 --> 18:05.293
Kidnapped him?

18:15.220 --> 18:16.805
[Gi-jeon] It traumatized him.

18:22.060 --> 18:23.353
[sighs]

18:25.605 --> 18:27.732
Oh… [sighs]

18:27.816 --> 18:29.317
[exhales sharply] Oh, dear. [whimpers]

18:30.735 --> 18:32.403
-What's wrong?
-[whimpers]

18:33.488 --> 18:34.906
[Young-hee] Mr. Ga Woo-su.

18:34.989 --> 18:37.116
This is the real world.

18:37.200 --> 18:39.911
People who know how to listen
survive longer

18:39.994 --> 18:43.623
than those who think being smart
is enough to get by.

18:43.706 --> 18:46.543
It's not like your face is going
to wear out just because we're filming it.

18:46.626 --> 18:48.711
Stop making such a fuss.

18:48.795 --> 18:50.964
-[inhales, sighs]
-[sighs]

18:52.382 --> 18:53.550
Please excuse me.

18:54.551 --> 18:56.678
If you're not willing to cooperate,

18:56.761 --> 18:59.222
you leave me with no choice.

19:06.771 --> 19:08.398
SUSPENSION NOTICE

19:09.065 --> 19:10.608
YOON DONG-JU

19:10.692 --> 19:13.736
I'm sure the other teachers
must have other options as well.

19:14.529 --> 19:16.656
But it'll be quite tough
for Mr. Yoon Dong-ju

19:16.739 --> 19:18.324
if he gets fired, right?

19:26.249 --> 19:28.209
[Woo-su] Now, we can see that negative 4

19:28.293 --> 19:30.461
is the average rate of change
in this equation.

19:30.545 --> 19:32.672
Next, we need to find the f prime of x.

19:32.755 --> 19:34.173
[chalk writing]

19:34.257 --> 19:35.633
Two x minus three.

19:35.717 --> 19:37.635
What's the average rate of change again?

19:37.719 --> 19:39.345
[students] Negative four.

19:40.722 --> 19:42.140
Yes, it's negative four.

19:46.269 --> 19:48.605
He could have just agreed
to the filming from the start.

19:48.688 --> 19:49.981
What was all that circus for?

19:51.107 --> 19:52.400
My point exactly.

19:52.483 --> 19:53.902
We're finishing late because of him.

19:53.985 --> 19:55.570
-[Woo-su] Therefore, the value of x is…
-What the heck is this?

19:55.653 --> 19:57.238
-So annoying.
-…is negative one-half.

19:57.322 --> 20:01.159
And negative one-half is a number
that falls between negative three and two.

20:04.162 --> 20:06.581
Therefore… [sighs] …c is…

20:09.083 --> 20:10.460
[sighs]

20:11.210 --> 20:12.921
We're finally done with it all.

20:13.004 --> 20:15.173
CHAPTER 25: I ONLY FEEL BETRAYED
BECAUSE I TRUSTED YOU

20:17.467 --> 20:19.218
[chuckles]

20:19.719 --> 20:21.095
[snores]

20:21.179 --> 20:23.222
[yawns]

20:23.306 --> 20:25.391
[groaning]

20:27.936 --> 20:29.938
[gasps] Auntie!

20:30.521 --> 20:32.440
What… What am I doing here?

20:32.523 --> 20:34.817
You said you couldn't sleep
at all last night

20:34.901 --> 20:36.277
and wanted to get rest.

20:36.361 --> 20:38.529
Were you asleep all along?

20:38.613 --> 20:40.615
I… I was?

20:41.407 --> 20:42.408
That makes no sense.

20:43.117 --> 20:44.160
And the show?

20:44.243 --> 20:46.579
They're done filming it all.

20:46.663 --> 20:47.664
What?

20:48.206 --> 20:49.624
[exclaims] Oh, no.

20:49.707 --> 20:51.793
[exclaims] Oh, no!

20:53.586 --> 20:56.255
No. No. Don't go. No. Please.

20:56.339 --> 20:59.175
Auntie, they're leaving.
They're actually leaving.

20:59.258 --> 21:00.635
They're leaving!

21:00.718 --> 21:03.137
No!

21:03.221 --> 21:05.223
[flute playing]

21:32.709 --> 21:34.293
[sighs]

21:34.377 --> 21:36.462
Just stop that!

21:46.764 --> 21:47.849
[sighs]

21:49.892 --> 21:51.769
[whimpers]

21:51.853 --> 21:53.312
[groans, sniffles]

21:53.938 --> 21:55.398
M-Mr. Ga.

21:58.234 --> 21:59.610
[breathes shakily]

21:59.694 --> 22:00.903
Mr. Ga.

22:13.499 --> 22:14.584
[breathes shakily]

22:27.388 --> 22:28.890
[breathes shakily] Well…

22:29.599 --> 22:30.975
Mr. Ga.

22:33.311 --> 22:35.188
Mr. Ga, I'm so sorry.

22:36.189 --> 22:39.817
I would have never taken a video of you
if I had known what you went through.

22:41.110 --> 22:42.111
I mean,

22:42.195 --> 22:44.363
I shouldn't have done it regardless.
I'm so sorry.

22:44.447 --> 22:47.158
It's my fault. I'm very, very sorry.

22:52.622 --> 22:54.165
[exhales sharply]

22:54.248 --> 22:56.209
You asked me a question during class.

22:57.210 --> 22:59.796
Guess what crossed my mind
in that split second.

23:03.508 --> 23:05.301
"Is she finally interested in math?"

23:11.599 --> 23:13.559
After hearing your question, I thought,

23:14.811 --> 23:16.312
"She may start with something unrelated.

23:17.688 --> 23:19.941
Maybe she'll gain
a little bit of interest in math

23:20.024 --> 23:21.818
once she hears
what I've been through in life."

23:22.693 --> 23:24.946
So I tried to give you an earnest answer.

23:27.198 --> 23:28.199
But you…

23:32.870 --> 23:33.913
[sighs]

23:34.956 --> 23:36.624
I felt let down

23:36.707 --> 23:38.501
because I put my trust in you.

23:40.545 --> 23:41.963
Forget it. Go home.

23:47.385 --> 23:49.178
Sorry for letting you down.

23:49.804 --> 23:52.181
I'm really sorry. [breathes shakily]

23:52.265 --> 23:53.266
Go.

23:54.684 --> 23:56.477
[breathes shakily]

24:02.066 --> 24:03.901
[winces]

24:04.819 --> 24:06.154
[groans]

24:07.321 --> 24:08.781
[whimpers]

24:11.033 --> 24:12.034
Get up.

24:13.077 --> 24:14.704
Your act isn't going to work.

24:15.371 --> 24:16.914
[Eui-ju inhales sharply]

24:16.998 --> 24:18.082
[grunting]

24:18.166 --> 24:22.003
[wincing]

24:22.086 --> 24:23.171
Eui-ju.

24:25.047 --> 24:26.048
Eui-ju.

24:28.050 --> 24:30.052
Eui-ju. Eui-ju.

24:30.136 --> 24:31.596
Wake up, Eui-ju!

24:32.763 --> 24:34.098
Eui-ju.

24:34.182 --> 24:35.349
Wake up, Eui-ju!

24:35.433 --> 24:37.685
[Eui-ju breathing heavily]

24:39.687 --> 24:41.397
[whimpering]

24:42.148 --> 24:44.442
[somber music playing]
